From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:30:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: Give paths, classes and query results what Windows
 gives them.

Measured on Windows 11 build 29671 with tools/winmgmtsprobe
(objectpath.vbs, classobject.vbs, locatable.c, contextprobe.c):

- A path to a class gives the class itself, of genus 1 with its
  properties all null, whether it has instances or not; a class that
  does not exist is not found.  A singleton's instance is Class=@.
- The system properties come in Windows' order, with __SUPERCLASS and
  __DYNASTY (null: there is no class hierarchy here).
- A query naming its properties gives results with no path, server or
  namespace, and a relative path when its keys are among them;
  WBEM_FLAG_ENSURE_LOCATABLE adds the keys and gives them all.
- A number compares with a string property as its digits: Win32_Process
  WHERE Handle = 4.
- A result's namespace is its own, ROOT\SecurityCenter2 and the others,
  not ROOT\CIMV2; a full path may name this machine as ".", and the
  connection's namespace.
- Devices' keys are spelled DeviceID.
- IWbemContext keeps its values in the order they were first set, and
  enumerates and deletes them; deleting a missing one is S_FALSE, Next
  outside an enumeration unexpected.

The tests check the paths of results and the context; on Windows they
have no failures (the query test's other failures there are its own).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

